 r←Test_Server_015(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;request;response;ind;key;uri
⍝ Requests the IndexNow key file and checks that the key switches the feature on and off
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed
 uri←TC.ReplaceRegistryAlias'[localhost]'

 ⍝ Without a key the feature is off, so not even "/.txt" is served:
 request←R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/.txt'
 response←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
 →T.PassesIf 404=response.StatusCode

 ⍝ Switch it on; the server reports the key it now uses:
 request←R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/v1/setindexnowkey'
 response←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
 →T.GoToTidyUp 200≠response.StatusCode
 key←response.Content
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=≢key

 ⍝ Now the key file is served, named after the key and holding just the key:
 request←R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/',key,'.txt'
 response←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
 →T.GoToTidyUp 200≠response.StatusCode
 →T.GoToTidyUp(≢response.Headers)<ind←(⊃¨response.Headers)⍳⊂'content-type'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'text/plain'⍷ind 2⊃response.Headers
 →T.GoToTidyUp key≢response.Content~⎕UCS 13 10

 ⍝ ... but only under exactly that name:
 request←R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/',key,'x.txt'
 response←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
 →T.GoToTidyUp 404≠response.StatusCode

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 request←R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/v1/unsetindexnowkey'
 response←TC.SendAndReceive uri request
 'Could not switch IndexNow off again'Assert 200=response.StatusCode
⍝Done
